\section{What an error bar here is not}{

The bars are built from \code{cells$se}, which is \code{sqrt(ms_error / n)} pooled over
the whole model, so a bar on a marginal mean over a set of cells has half-width
\code{sqrt(sum(se^2) / length(se)^2)} times one or the \code{qt()} multiplier. That is
the standard error of the mean being drawn, not of the difference between two
of them, and the difference is what the interaction is about. Two bars that
overlap do not settle the term test, which is in \verb{$terms}, and two points whose
gap you want tested are in \verb{$posthoc}.
}

